# Diagnostic-only. Do not install as a product default.
#
# Intended later A/B (Phase B), after W0 already shows wrap:
#
#   [/bass.dll]
#   BOX64_DYNAREC=0
#
# This Box64 fork stores per-file env on the mapping, but FillBlock/DBGetBlock
# gate dynarec with the *global* BOX64ENV(dynarec). BOX64DRENV(dynarec) is never
# read. So [/bass.dll] BOX64_DYNAREC=0 is currently NOT a reliable way to force
# BASS onto the interpreter.
#
# Before using this file, confirm in Box64 logs that bass.dll actually received
# a per-file env ("Applied [/bass.dll] ..." / Mapping of ... bass.dll) AND that
# no dynablocks are created in that range.
#
# If per-file DYNAREC=0 does not skip FillBlock, Phase B must use process-wide:
#
#   BOX64_DYNAREC=0
#
# which will slow the whole Wine/M5 session.
#
# Copy to $HOME/.box64rc only for a measured A/B, then remove it.

[/bass.dll]
BOX64_DYNAREC=0
